+# rev0841 change summary
+
+## Main risk addressed
+
+rev0841 addresses review-layer and packaging-hygiene issues found while reading the rev0840 overlay deeply. It does not alter the rev0840 publication-rights code changes, does not invent any license terms, and does not claim canonical publication readiness.
+
+## Code/content changes
+
+- Added `SESSION_REVIEW_REV0841.md` and `SESSION_REVIEW_REV0841.json` with prioritized findings about rights, identity, provenance, RO-Crate/SPDX, citation metadata, and cloudtainer waste.
+- Added `AUDIT/OVERLAY_ABSOLUTE_PATH_REFERENCE_AUDIT_REV0841.md` and `.json` to audit the overlay artifact itself for cloud/container absolute path references.
+- Added `CHECKS/patch-bundle-identity-rev0841.json` so the bundle identity is explicit: rev0841 overlay/review bundle carrying rev0840 patch streams and rev0826 canonical release surfaces.
+- Normalized `CHECKS/input-artifacts.sha256` from cloudtainer-local absolute input paths to input archive basenames.
+- Refreshed `CHECKS/overlay-manifest.json` and `CHECKS/overlay-manifest.sha256`.
+
+## Deliberately unchanged
+
+- `PATCHES/rev0826-to-rev0840-cumulative.patch` and `PATCHES/rev0839-to-rev0840-incremental.patch` were left unchanged so existing patch validation remains interpretable.
+- Canonical-tree surfaces (`MANIFEST.sha256`, `INDEX/files.*`, `RELEASE_MANIFEST.json`, RO-Crate metadata, SPDX inventory, rights ledgers) were not silently rewritten as rev0841 canonical release surfaces.
+
+## Rights status
+
+Still publication-blocked. rev0841 records the issue; it does not resolve licensing/notice decisions.
+
+---
